<title>USA: U.S. mortgage refinancing volume up 53.3 pct.</title>
<headline>U.S. mortgage refinancing volume up 53.3 pct.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The volume of U.S. mortgage refinancing applications jumped 53.3 percent in the week ended July 11, according to a Mortgage Bankers Association of America weekly survey.</p>
<p>The total volume of mortgage applications gained 29.6 percent in the latest survey week, while applications to purchase mortgages increased 22.5 percent.</p>
<p>The seasonally adjusted refinancing index rose 22.7 percent to 497.3 from a revised 405.4 percent the previous week. The purchase index dipped 2.6 percent to 212.9 in the latest survey from 218.6 in the previous week.  </p>
